isableActiveStateStyles-Wa6TmGN3 apply-overflow-tooltip apply-overflow-tooltip--check-children-recursively apply-overflow-tooltip--allow-text\"><span class=\"content-Wa6TmGN3\">Dividends</span></button><button role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-selected=\"false\" aria-disabled=\"false\" id=\"Ipo\" data-overflow-tooltip-text=\"IPO\" class=\"roundTabButton-Wa6TmGN3 small-Wa6TmGN3 primary-Wa6TmGN3 disableActiveStateStyles-Wa6TmGN3 apply-overflow-tooltip apply-overflow-tooltip--check-children-recursively apply-overflow-tooltip--allow-text\"><span class=\"content-Wa6TmGN3\">IPO</span></button><button aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-overflow-tooltip-text=\"More\" class=\"roundTabButton-Wa6TmGN3 small-Wa6TmGN3 primary-Wa6TmGN3 withStartIcon-Wa6TmGN3 iconOnly-Wa6TmGN3 fake-Wa6TmGN3 disableActiveStateStyles-Wa6TmGN3 apply-overflow-tooltip apply-overflow-tooltip--check-children-recursively apply-overflow-tooltip--allow-text\"><span role=\"img\" class=\"startIconWrap-Wa6TmGN3\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 28 28\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M9 14a3 3 0 1 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1 6 0zm8 0a3 3 0 1 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1 6 0zm5 3a3 3 0 1 0 0-6 3 3 0 0 0 0 6z\"/></svg></span><span class=\"content-Wa6TmGN3 visuallyHidden-Wa6TmGN3\">More</span></button></div></div></div><div class=\"wrapper-hct2yJvK animated-hct2yJvK\"><div class=\"wrapper-aDcS4leG filtersSkeleton-Gse8UENY\"></div></div></div></div><div class=\"content-Gse8UENY\"><div class=\"content-TmOQi8pO idleContent-TmOQi8pO\" data-name=\"economic-calendar\"><div class=\"tv-spinner tv-spinner--shown tv-spinner--size_large\" role=\"progressbar\"></div></div></div><div class=\"infoBlock-UJOoxe7w\"><h2 class=\"title-UJOoxe7w\">How to use Economic Calendar</h2><div class=\"text-UJOoxe7w\"><p class=\"paragraph-UJOoxe7w\">Economic Calendar on TradingView shows the latest and upcoming economic events that can affect certain assets, regions, and global markets — for example, <a class=\"primary-luAmB0cV\" href=\"/markets/stocks-usa/market-movers-all-stocks/\" target=\"_blank\">stocks</a>, <a class=\"primary-luAmB0cV\" href=\"/markets/currencies/rates-all/\" target=\"_blank\">Forex</a>, or <a class=\"primary-luAmB0cV\" href=\"/markets/bonds/prices-all/\" target=\"_blank\">bonds</a>.</p><p class=\"paragraph-UJOoxe7w\">All events are in chronological order and linked with <a class=\"primary-luAmB0cV\" href=\"/markets/world-economy/indicators/gdp/\" target=\"_blank\">economic indicators</a> like interest rates or GDP. The calendar is customizable: one click will give you a weekly economic calendar, another — narrow it down to US economic calendar only. Plus, you will see short explainers of the events and forecasts from experts. Just set your calendar and prepare for the next trade.</p><p class=\"paragraph-UJOoxe7w\">Learn more about the Economic Calendar features in our <a class=\"primary-luAmB0cV\" href=\"?solution=43000707391\" target=\"_blank\">Help Center</a>.</p></div><div class=\"faqSection-UJOoxe7w\"><div data-base-widget=\"true\" data-container-name=\"calendars-faq-widget-id\" data-an-widget-id=\"calendars-faq-widget-id\" class=\"container-tRBrMTYb\"><div class=\"header-tRBrMTYb header-l-tRBrMTYb\"><div class=\"wrapper-QjjAoTcT center-QjjAoTcT wrap-QjjAoTcT\"><span class=\"titleAndHintWrapper-QjjAoTcT truncated-QjjAoTcT\"><div class=\"container-QjjAoTcT\"><h2 class=\"title-QjjAoTcT title-l-QjjAoTcT\" id=\"calendars-faq-widget-id\">Frequently asked questions</h2>﻿</div></span></div></div><div class=\"content-tRBrMTYb\" data-qa-id=\"calendars-faq-widget-id-content\"><div class=\"wrapper-QsoWdXNj twoColumns-QsoWdXNj\"><div class=\"column-QsoWdXNj\"><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:0\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::R2qm:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::R2qm:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What is the Economic Calendar?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::R2qm:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">The Economic Calendar is a tool featuring dates for important economic events and releases that could potentially influence specific asset prices or whole markets.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:2\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::R4qm:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::R4qm:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">How to trade with the Economic Calendar?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::R4qm:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">The Economic Calendar is a versatile tool. You can use it for research — it is important to know what&#x27;s going on within the financial markets and sectors where you have positions. You can also learn about economic indicators and what they can affect. In our Calendar, you can compare actual and historical data and see the divergence from the forecast to better understand trends. All this can help you design more event-driven strategies that will easily adapt to changes in the global economy.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:4\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::R6qm:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::R6qm:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">How to filter events in the Economic Calendar?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::R6qm:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">Several filters can make working with the Economic Calendar easier. First, you can choose the period: select the necessary week in the Calendar on the upper toolbar or pick a specific day. Then, you can select the countries and time zones to sync events with your strategy needs. Lastly, you can filter events by their importance and even limit the event flow by a specific category to see only GDP releases or tax announcements.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:6\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::R8qm:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::R8qm:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are main UK events to look out for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::R8qm:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">One of the leading European economies, the UK is also one of the world&#x27;s financial centres attracting traders worldwide. You can closely watch the UK economy on our Economic Calendar. Here are some key indicators to look for.<br/>- GDP, a universal measure of an economy&#x27;s strength.<br/>- Indicators measuring production: industrial production and manufacturing production.<br/>- BoE interest rate decision defining the repo rate applied to open market operations of the Bank of England with a group of counterparties (banks, building societies, securities firms).<br/>- Employment data, measured by the unemployment rate, claimant count, etc., coming from the Labor Market Overview report released monthly by the Office for National Statistics.<br/>- Inflation and core inflation.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:8\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Raqm:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Raqm:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are main EU events to look out for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Raqm:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">Comprised of many versatile countries, the EU plays a key role in the global economy. Here are some of the main indicators to watch when analyzing the European Union&#x27;s economy.<br/>- EU GDP or GDP growth to see the indicator&#x27;s dynamics.<br/>- Interest rate, the most convenient way to watch it is to track ECB interest rate decision.<br/>- EU inflation.<br/>- EU ZEW index, measuring the level of optimism that analysts have about the expected economic developments over the next six months.<br/>- CPI.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:10\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Rcqm:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Rcqm:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are main events in France to look out for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Rcqm:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">France boasts one of the biggest economies worldwide, and here are some key economic events that can help you track its growth:<br/>- The one and only GDP.<br/>- Employment indicators such as unemployment rate, benefits, jobseekers, and others.<br/>- Inflation rate.<br/>- Exports — mostly comprised of transport equipment, mechanical equipment, chemicals, perfumes, cosmetics, and other export categories.<br/>- Balance of trade.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:12\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Reqm:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Reqm:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are main events in Brazil to look out for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Reqm:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">Boasting both an abundance of natural resources and people, Brazil economy is one of the largest in the world and the second one in Americas, so many traders track its dynamics. Here are some key indicators to follow.<br/>- Brazil GDP.<br/>- GDP growth, to evaluate the key indicator in its dynamics.<br/>- BCB interest rate decision.<br/>- Inflation rate, closely tied to markets.<br/>- Unemployment rate.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:14\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Rgqm:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Rgqm:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What is the US interest rate?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Rgqm:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">US current interest rate is <!-- -->3.75<!-- -->%.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul isLastInColumn-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:16\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Riqm:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Riqm:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What is the US inflation rate?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Riqm:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">The last reported US inflation rate (<!-- -->Aug 12, 2026<!-- -->) is <!-- -->3.4<!-- -->%.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"column-QsoWdXNj\"><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:1\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::R3am:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::R3am:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">How many countries does the Economic Calendar provide events for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::R3am:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">The Calendar provides more than 300,000 economic indicators from over 190 countries, but you can choose to show events for selected countries only or display releases from G20 members.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:3\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::R5am:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::R5am:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are key economic indicators globally?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::R5am:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">Traders usually watch indicators that can affect their strategies, but there are also some indicators that influence global markets in general and, consequently, everyone&#x27;s strategies. Here are some of the major indicators that all traders should look out for.<br/>- GDP. Measuring the market value of all the final goods and services produced in a country over a specific period. It can help you understand how well a country&#x27;s economy is performing and provide insight into its stock market. An expanding economy can positively influence stock prices.<br/>- Interest rate. The amount charged by a lender (central bank) usually has an inverse relationship with the stock markets. When interest rates rise, share prices fall, and bonds become more attractive.<br/>- Consumer Price Index (CPI). Gauges the general fluctuation in consumer prices. It&#x27;s widely embraced as the primary indicator of inflation and tracked by many traders as increased CPI suggests increased inflation and a chance of a market downtrend.<br/>- Consumer Confidence Index (CCI). Measures consumer sentiment about the economy and personal financial security. Higher value typically leads to increased spending, driving economic growth.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:5\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::R7am:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::R7am:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are main US events to look out for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::R7am:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">In addition to the company data, it&#x27;s crucial to track the overall state of the country&#x27;s economy, especially when it comes to one of the world leaders. Here are some of the economic indicators that can help you evaluate the US economy.<br/>- GDP. Calculated by the Bureau of Economic Analysis with data gathered by the Bureau of Labor Statistics. In our calendar, you can track it with the GDP growth rate value.<br/>- Fed interest rate decisions.<br/>- Employment figures. These include the unemployment rate, payrolls, and job openings.<br/>- Indicators measuring inflation, such as Consumer Price Index (CPI) and Producer Price Index (PPI).<br/>- Industrial production, measuring the output of manufacturing-based industries.<br/>- Consumer behaviour with personal spending and income indicators. It helps gauge consumer spending health.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:7\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::R9am:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::R9am:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are main events in Canada to look out for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::R9am:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">Highly developed and one of the largest in the world, the Canadian economy is watched by traders worldwide, and there are a few key indicators to follow.<br/>- Canada GDP.<br/>- BoC interest rate decision.<br/>- BoC monetary policy report.<br/>- Employment figures, including unemployment rate and employment change.<br/>- Canada exports, the biggest export products are energy, crude oil and crude bitumen, cars and parts, and consumer goods.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:9\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Rbam:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Rbam:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are main events in Germany to look out for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Rbam:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">Germany represents one of Europe&#x27;s key economies. Below are the main economic events to help you follow the German economy:<br/>- Germany GDP.<br/>- GDP growth.<br/>- Unemployment figures, including unemployment rate, change, and unemployed persons.<br/>- Inflation rate.<br/>- German exports, with the main exports being motor vehicles, machinery and equipment, chemicals, computers, electronic and optical products, pharmaceutical products, etc.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:11\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Rdam:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Rdam:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are main events in Japan to look out for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Rdam:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">A country with a big economy, Japan attracts investors worldwide. Here are some key economic events that will help you evaluate the Japanese economy:<br/>- GDP growth, to understand GDP in dynamics.<br/>- Inflation.<br/>- Japan exports, including vehicles, machinery, and electronics, and imports of mineral fuels, electronic equipment, and machinery.<br/>- Unemployment rate.<br/>- Bank of Japan interest rate decision and other announcements, meeting minutes and executives&#x27; speeches.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:13\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Rfam:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Rfam:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What are main events in China to look out for?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Rfam:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">One of the global economy pillars, China&#x27;s economy is large and versatile. Here are a few key indicators that will help you track its performance.<br/>- China&#x27;s GDP and GDP growth.<br/>- China exports and imports. Electronic and transport equipment make up the largest part of exports, while integrated circuits and crude oil are China&#x27;s largest imports.<br/>- Unemployment rate.<br/>- Inflation rate.<br/>- China Foreign Direct Investment (FDI), which is foreign capital actually utilized.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:15\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Rham:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Rham:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What is the US GDP?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Rham:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">US GDP reached <!-- -->‪30.77 T‬<!-- --> <!-- -->USD<!-- --> in <!-- -->2025<!-- -->.</div></div></div><div class=\"item-dQ0apaul medium-dQ0apaul isLastInColumn-dQ0apaul isLast-dQ0apaul\" style=\"order:17\"><button class=\"summary-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-summary::Rjam:\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"Accordion-details::Rjam:\"><div class=\"summaryLine-dQ0apaul\"><span class=\"background-dQ0apaul\"></span><div class=\"summaryText-dQ0apaul\">What is the US unemployment rate?</div><div role=\"presentation\"><div class=\"wrapper-HyXauJWC medium-HyXauJWC\"><div class=\"horizontal-HyXauJWC\"></div><div class=\"vertical-HyXauJWC\"></div></div></div></div></button><div class=\"detailsWrapper-dQ0apaul\" id=\"Accordion-details::Rjam:\" inert=\"\"><div class=\"details-dQ0apaul\">As of <!-- -->Aug 7, 2026<!-- -->, US unemployment rate is <!-- -->4.1<!-- -->%.</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><script type=\"application/prs.init-data+json\">{\"64ZhD9\":{\"faq_data\":{\"economic\":[{\"question\":\"What is the Economic Calendar?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"The Economic Calendar is a tool featuring dates for important economic events and releases that could potentially influence specific asset prices or whole markets.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{}},{\"question\":\"How many countries does the Economic Calendar provide events for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"The Calendar provides more than 300,000 economic indicators from over 190 countries, but you can choose to show events for selected countries only or display releases from G20 members.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{}},{\"question\":\"How to trade with the Economic Calendar?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"The Economic Calendar is a versatile tool. You can use it for research — it is important to know what's going on within the financial markets and sectors where you have positions. You can also learn about economic indicators and what they can affect. In our Calendar, you can compare actual and historical data and see the divergence from the forecast to better understand trends. All this can help you design more event-driven strategies that will easily adapt to changes in the global economy.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{}},{\"question\":\"What are key economic indicators globally?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Traders usually watch indicators that can affect their strategies, but there are also some indicators that influence global markets in general and, consequently, everyone's strategies. Here are some of the major indicators that all traders should look out for.{br}- GDP. Measuring the market value of all the final goods and services produced in a country over a specific period. It can help you understand how well a country's economy is performing and provide insight into its stock market. An expanding economy can positively influence stock prices.{br}- Interest rate. The amount charged by a lender (central bank) usually has an inverse relationship with the stock markets. When interest rates rise, share prices fall, and bonds become more attractive.{br}- Consumer Price Index (CPI). Gauges the general fluctuation in consumer prices. It's widely embraced as the primary indicator of inflation and tracked by many traders as increased CPI suggests increased inflation and a chance of a market downtrend.{br}- Consumer Confidence Index (CCI). Measures consumer sentiment about the economy and personal financial security. Higher value typically leads to increased spending, driving economic growth.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"How to filter events in the Economic Calendar?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Several filters can make working with the Economic Calendar easier. First, you can choose the period: select the necessary week in the Calendar on the upper toolbar or pick a specific day. Then, you can select the countries and time zones to sync events with your strategy needs. Lastly, you can filter events by their importance and even limit the event flow by a specific category to see only GDP releases or tax announcements.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{}},{\"question\":\"What are main US events to look out for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"In addition to the company data, it's crucial to track the overall state of the country's economy, especially when it comes to one of the world leaders. Here are some of the economic indicators that can help you evaluate the US economy.{br}- GDP. Calculated by the Bureau of Economic Analysis with data gathered by the Bureau of Labor Statistics. In our calendar, you can track it with the GDP growth rate value.{br}- Fed interest rate decisions.{br}- Employment figures. These include the unemployment rate, payrolls, and job openings.{br}- Indicators measuring inflation, such as Consumer Price Index (CPI) and Producer Price Index (PPI).{br}- Industrial production, measuring the output of manufacturing-based industries.{br}- Consumer behaviour with personal spending and income indicators. It helps gauge consumer spending health.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What are main UK events to look out for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"One of the leading European economies, the UK is also one of the world's financial centres attracting traders worldwide. You can closely watch the UK economy on our Economic Calendar. Here are some key indicators to look for.{br}- GDP, a universal measure of an economy's strength.{br}- Indicators measuring production: industrial production and manufacturing production.{br}- BoE interest rate decision defining the repo rate applied to open market operations of the Bank of England with a group of counterparties (banks, building societies, securities firms).{br}- Employment data, measured by the unemployment rate, claimant count, etc., coming from the Labor Market Overview report released monthly by the Office for National Statistics.{br}- Inflation and core inflation.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What are main events in Canada to look out for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Highly developed and one of the largest in the world, the Canadian economy is watched by traders worldwide, and there are a few key indicators to follow.{br}- Canada GDP.{br}- BoC interest rate decision.{br}- BoC monetary policy report.{br}- Employment figures, including unemployment rate and employment change.{br}- Canada exports, the biggest export products are energy, crude oil and crude bitumen, cars and parts, and consumer goods.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What are main EU events to look out for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Comprised of many versatile countries, the EU plays a key role in the global economy. Here are some of the main indicators to watch when analyzing the European Union's economy.{br}- EU GDP or GDP growth to see the indicator's dynamics.{br}- Interest rate, the most convenient way to watch it is to track ECB interest rate decision.{br}- EU inflation.{br}- EU ZEW index, measuring the level of optimism that analysts have about the expected economic developments over the next six months.{br}- CPI.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What are main events in Germany to look out for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Germany represents one of Europe's key economies. Below are the main economic events to help you follow the German economy:{br}- Germany GDP.{br}- GDP growth.{br}- Unemployment figures, including unemployment rate, change, and unemployed persons.{br}- Inflation rate.{br}- German exports, with the main exports being motor vehicles, machinery and equipment, chemicals, computers, electronic and optical products, pharmaceutical products, etc.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What are main events in France to look out for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"France boasts one of the biggest economies worldwide, and here are some key economic events that can help you track its growth:{br}- The one and only GDP.{br}- Employment indicators such as unemployment rate, benefits, jobseekers, and others.{br}- Inflation rate.{br}- Exports — mostly comprised of transport equipment, mechanical equipment, chemicals, perfumes, cosmetics, and other export categories.{br}- Balance of trade.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What are main events in Japan to look out for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"A country with a big economy, Japan attracts investors worldwide. Here are some key economic events that will help you evaluate the Japanese economy:{br}- GDP growth, to understand GDP in dynamics.{br}- Inflation.{br}- Japan exports, including vehicles, machinery, and electronics, and imports of mineral fuels, electronic equipment, and machinery.{br}- Unemployment rate.{br}- Bank of Japan interest rate decision and other announcements, meeting minutes and executives' speeches.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What are main events in Brazil to look out for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Boasting both an abundance of natural resources and people, Brazil economy is one of the largest in the world and the second one in Americas, so many traders track its dynamics. Here are some key indicators to follow.{br}- Brazil GDP.{br}- GDP growth, to evaluate the key indicator in its dynamics.{br}- BCB interest rate decision.{br}- Inflation rate, closely tied to markets.{br}- Unemployment rate.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What are main events in China to look out for?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"One of the global economy pillars, China's economy is large and versatile. Here are a few key indicators that will help you track its performance.{br}- China's GDP and GDP growth.{br}- China exports and imports. Electronic and transport equipment make up the largest part of exports, while integrated circuits and crude oil are China's largest imports.{br}- Unemployment rate.{br}- Inflation rate.{br}- China Foreign Direct Investment (FDI), which is foreign capital actually utilized.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What is the US interest rate?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"US current interest rate is {us_intr_last_price}%.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"us_intr_last_price\":{\"renderer\":null,\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"us_intr_last_price\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":3.75,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]}}},{\"question\":\"What is the US GDP?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"US GDP reached {us_gdb_last_price}{nbsp}{us_gdp_currency_code} in {us_gdp_reference_last_period}.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"us_gdb_last_price\":{\"renderer\":\"financial\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"us_gdb_last_price\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":30769700000000,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"us_gdp_currency_code\":{\"renderer\":\"currency\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"us_gdp_currency_code\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"USD\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"us_gdp_reference_last_period\":{\"renderer\":null,\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"us_gdp_reference_last_period\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"2025\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"nbsp\":{\"renderer\":\"nbsp\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What is the US inflation rate?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"The last reported US inflation rate ({us_iryy_last_release_date}) is {us_iryy_last_price}%.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"us_iryy_last_release_date\":{\"renderer\":\"date\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"us_iryy_last_release_date\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":1786537800,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"us_iryy_last_price\":{\"renderer\":null,\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"us_iryy_last_price\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":3.4,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]}}},{\"question\":\"What is the US unemployment rate?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"As of {us_ur_last_release_date}, US unemployment rate is {us_ur_last_price}%.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"us_ur_last_release_date\":{\"renderer\":\"date\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"us_ur_last_release_date\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":1786105800,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"us_ur_last_price\":{\"renderer\":null,\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"us_ur_last_price\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":4.1,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]}}}],\"earnings\":[{\"question\":\"What is the Earnings Calendar?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Earnings Calendar is a tool to track companies' earnings in a convenient table with key data.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{}},{\"question\":\"What are earnings?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Earnings are a company's after-tax net income. When it comes to earnings, investors usually track a more specific indicator — earnings per share, which is the amount of earnings per share issued. It helps them better understand the potential of the future investment.{br}{br}Earnings reports are released quarterly, semi-annually, or annually. They usually make up earnings seasons or time periods when a large number of publicly traded companies release earnings.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"How can earnings influence stock prices?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"As a crucial indicator of a company's financial health, earnings tend to drive stock prices, with strong earnings pushing stock prices higher. On the contrary, declining earnings may signal a decrease in the company's share price. With the Earnings Calendar, you can keep an eye on EPS estimates, actual value, and surprises to adjust your strategy on time. For example, when earnings exceed estimates, traders may feel confident in the company's future and want to buy its shares.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{}},{\"question\":\"What are the {title} earnings?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"The {title} last reported earnings are {earnings_last_actual}{nbsp}{currency} — the estimate was {earnings_last_estimate}{nbsp}{currency}, which resulted in {earnings_last_surprise}% surprise. The next report is planned for {earnings_release_next_date}. Track the {earnings_page_link_start}{title} earnings{link_end} in more detail to make informed decisions.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"currency\":{\"renderer\":null,\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"currency\",\"source\":\"django_model\",\"value\":\"USD\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"title\":{\"renderer\":null,\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"instrument_name\",\"source\":\"django_model\",\"value\":\"Alphabet Inc (Google) Class C\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"earnings_last_actual\":{\"renderer\":\"financial\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"fundamental_earnings_last_actual\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":9.11,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"earnings_last