t be paid the next dividend payment. The ex-date usually comes one day before the record date.{br}{br}Tracking the ex-dividend date may also be useful as the stock price usually falls after reaching it — this highlights the fact that new shareholders won't be entitled to that dividend payment.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"How are dividends taxed?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Dividend income tax rates vary and depend on the country's tax regulations and the stock's listing. In the US, dividend income can be taxed by the IRS in various ways. Many factors are considered when forming the rate, but generally, the tax depends on the income amount and type.{br}- Qualified dividends are taxed at the rate of 0%, 15% or 20%, depending on taxable income and filing status. These are regular dividends paid by a US company or a qualified foreign company with stock held for more than 60 days within the 121-day period around the ex-dividend date.{br}- Non-qualified (ordinary) dividends are taxed at an ordinary income tax rate ranging from 10% to 37%, depending on income level.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What's the best dividend stock?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Stock markets are prone to changes, so the highest-dividend stocks may vary. Right now, {highest_dividend_yield_in_america_company_title} has the highest dividend yield on the US market. Track more {high_yielding_stocks_link_start}high-yielding stocks{link_end} to find new opportunities.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"highest_dividend_yield_in_america_company_title\":{\"renderer\":null,\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"highest_dividend_yield_in_america_company_title\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"HeartCore Enterprises, Inc.\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"high_yielding_stocks_link_start\":{\"renderer\":\"link\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"high_yielding_stocks_link\",\"sour