me\":\"instrument_name\",\"source\":\"django_model\",\"value\":\"Amazon.com, Inc.\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"dividends_last_actual\":{\"renderer\":\"financial\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"dividend_amount_recent\",\"source\":\"django_model\",\"value\":null,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"dividends_yield\":{\"renderer\":\"financial\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"dividends_yield_current\",\"source\":\"django_model\",\"value\":0.0,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"dividends_page_link_start\":{\"renderer\":\"link\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"symbol_financials_dividends_link\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"/symbols/NASDAQ-AMZN/financials-dividends/\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"dividends_availability\":{\"renderer\":null,\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"dividends_availability\",\"source\":\"django_model\",\"value\":-1,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"nbsp\":{\"renderer\":\"nbsp\",\"fields\":null}}}],\"ipo\":[{\"question\":\"What is an IPO?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"An Initial Public Offering (IPO) is when a private company starts selling its shares to the public for the first time on a stock exchange. In other words, it’s an event of 'going public' — a company gets listed on an exchange and becomes accessible to common investors.{br}{br}Through an IPO, a company raises capital that it later uses to fuel growth, pay off debt, or expand its operations. For investors, it’s a chance to buy shares in a business at the start of its 'public' life and then profit from the stock price growth later.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null}}},{\"question\":\"What are IPO stocks?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"IPO stocks are shares of a company that have just gone public through an Initial Public Offering (IPO). When a private company becomes available to the public, it lists its stocks on an exchange, so that everyday investors have the chance to buy into the business early.{br}{br}These stocks often attract attention because they can offer high growth potential. At the same time, they pose higher risks, because the company’s performance on the market is untested and can change dramatically.{br}{br}That’s why IPOs are often featured among {stock_market_movers_link_start}stock market movers{link_end}, drawing interest from traders looking for new opportunities.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null},\"stock_market_movers_link_start\":{\"renderer\":\"link\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"stock_market_movers_link\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"/markets/stocks-usa/market-movers-all-stocks/\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]}}},{\"question\":\"How to invest in an IPO?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"The easiest way is to track market news, prepare for an IPO, and buy a company's stocks after it goes public. But you can start the process earlier and secure the shares you want to buy:{br}{br}- {bold_start}Check if you're eligible.{bold_end} Not all investors can access IPO shares. Some brokerages require a certain account size, trading history, or risk profile.{br}- {bold_start}Open an account with a broker.{bold_end} You’ll need a particular brokerage that takes part in IPO allocations.{br}- {bold_start}Review the prospectus document.{bold_end} It explains the company’s business, financials, risks, and goals for raising capital. It'll help you make an informed decision.{br}- {bold_start}Indicate your interest.{bold_end} Before the IPO, investors can request a certain number of shares through their broker.{br}- {bold_start}Wait for allocation.{bold_end} Once allocated, those shares are yours at the IPO price. Note: if demand is high, you may receive fewer shares than you requested — or even none.{br}- {bold_start}Trade.{bold_end} Once the company goes live, you can buy shares just like any other stock.{br}{br}Remember: always do your research first and {paper_trading_link_start}test your trading skills{link_end} before committing real capital.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"bold_start\":{\"renderer\":\"bold\",\"fields\":null},\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null},\"paper_trading_link_start\":{\"renderer\":\"link\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"paper_trading_link\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"/support/solutions/43000516466-paper-trading-main-functionality/\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]}}},{\"question\":\"Should I buy IPO stocks?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Buying IPO stocks can give investors the chance to get in early on a company’s public life. If the business grows, early shareholders may see significant gains. Imagine buying Apple's stock back in 1980. IPOs also generate a lot of buzz, which can lead to quick price jumps on the first day of trading.{br}{br}At the same time, IPO stocks can be very risky. Prices can be highly volatile in the early days, often moving more on hype than fundamentals. Plus, many companies are still unproven at scale, and some IPOs underperform after the initial excitement fades.{br}{br}So, just like any other investment strategy, investing in IPO can bring gains, but it goes along with many risks, so it's crucial to perform a thorough analysis before committing real money. Track {latest_news_link_start}latest news{link_end}, read {trading_ideas_link_start}trading ideas{link_end} to know what other traders think, and more — all on TradingView.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null},\"latest_news_link_start\":{\"renderer\":\"link\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"latest_news_link\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"/news/\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"trading_ideas_link_start\":{\"renderer\":\"link\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"trading_ideas_link\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"/ideas/\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]}}},{\"question\":\"How to buy pre-IPO stocks?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"Buying pre-IPO stocks is more complicated than buying shares of a public company. They are typically sold during private funding rounds to venture capital firms, institutional investors, or accredited individuals, so even if you find a specialized broker, you may need to meet income or net worth thresholds. There are some alternatives if you are willing to access a private company:{br}{br}- {bold_start}Secondary marketplaces{bold_end}. Accredited investors can purchase shares of pre-IPO companies directly from employees or existing shareholders.{br}- {bold_start}{etf_link_start}ETFs{link_end}{bold_end}. Simply invest in funds that already have access to pre-IPO stocks.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null},\"bold_start\":{\"renderer\":\"bold\",\"fields\":null},\"etf_link_start\":{\"renderer\":\"link\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"etf_link\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"/markets/etfs/funds-largest/\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]}}},{\"question\":\"What's the largest IPO in history?\",\"answer\":[{\"text\":\"As of {current_year}, the largest and most successful IPO was conducted by Saudi Aramco. During its IPO, Aramco raised $25.6 billion through the sale of 3 billion shares. Later, it reportedly sold 450 million more shares and increased the amount raised to $29.4 billion. With these numbers, Saudi Aramco surpassed Alibaba and became the largest IPO in world history.{br}Make use of our {news_flow_link_start}News Flow{link_end} to keep an eye on global market insights and spot the appearance of the next stock giant.\",\"filter\":null}],\"variables\":{\"br\":{\"renderer\":\"br\",\"fields\":null},\"news_flow_link_start\":{\"renderer\":\"link\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"news_flow_link\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":\"/news-flow/\",\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]},\"current_year\":{\"renderer\":\"dateYear\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"current_timestamp\",\"source\":\"django_seo\",\"value\":1787968593.1998723,\"origin_field_name\":null,\"symbol\":null}]}}}]},\"location\":\"/economic-calendar/\",\"seo_data\":{\"economic\":{\"page_title\":\"Economic Calendar — World Economic Events\",\"meta_description\":\"Explore the global and US Economic Calendar this week. Track economic news and monitor updates on GDP, interest rates, unemployment rates, and inflation data.\",\"image_file_name\":\"economic.jpg\"},\"earnings\":{\"page_title\":\"Earnings Calendar This Week — Upcoming Reports\",\"meta_description\":\"Track earnings reports today and in the upcoming weeks with our Earnings Calendar. View estimated and actual EPS, market cap, and earnings surprise.\",\"image_file_name\":\"earnings.jpg\"},\"dividend\":{\"page_title\":\"Dividend Calendar — Ex-Date, Yield, and More\",\"meta_description\":\"Track reports of dividend stocks with our calendar. Analyze ex-dividend dates, dividend yield, and other data to find the most promising stocks on the global markets.\",\"image_file_name\":\"dividend.jpg\"},\"ipo\":{\"page_title\":\"IPO Calendar — Upcoming & Recent IPOs\",\"meta_description\":\"Track upcoming IPOs with our IPO Calendar. See all initial public offerings, listing dates, number of shares, and more to find new companies to invest in.\",\"image_file_name\":\"ipo.jpg\"}},\"ssrTimeSeconds\":1787968593.2179546}}</script>\n\n</div>\n\t\t\t</main>\t\t</div>\n\n<script nonce=\"IVAM7Z6ZHE21lNj2T4Vjhg==\">window.fbAppId = \"155037361239837\";</script>\n\t<script nonce=\"IVAM7Z6ZHE21lNj2T4Vjhg==\">window.BLOG_LOCALIZED_URL = \"https://www.tradingview.com/blog/en/\";\n\n\n\t\t\tinitData.idc_exchanges_list = [\"nzx\",\"bme\",\"bme_stocks\",\"shfe\",\"szse\",\"nag\",\"tfx\",\"twse\",\"bvc\",\"bvcv\",\"bmv\",\"bvmt\",\"bvl\",\"bcs\",\"six\",\"bsse\",\"bahrain\",\"belex\",\"nseke\",\"qse\"];\n\n\t\t\tinitData.idc_delay_exchanges_list = [\"shfe\",\"tfx\",\"bvcv\",\"bvmt\",\"bsse\",\"bahrain\"];\n\n\t\t\tinitData.offlineAlertEventsOnInit = true;\n\n\n</script>\n\t\t<script type=\"application/prs.init-data+json\">\n